# A pattern here is matched against the path from the context root, as Go's filepath.Match
# does: `__pycache__` alone leaves out a directory of that name at the root and no other, so
# what may sit at any depth is written `**/` (#1141).
#
# The two `src/postulo/jobs/data` lines are what `manage.py fetch_esco` and `fetch_geonames`
# download into a working tree, 71 MB that `COPY src` carried into an image built from one,
# where nothing reads it: the image keeps both under /app/data. The licence notes and the
# NACE table beside them are committed and are not matched (`tests/test_ignore_files.py`).
.git
.github
.forgejo
.venv
**/node_modules
data
src/postulo/jobs/data/esco-*
src/postulo/jobs/data/geonames-*
staticfiles
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.sqlite3
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
tests
docs
scripts
!scripts/messages.py
